# ThreadSanitizer suppressions.
#
# Wired into the tsan build only, via gtest_discover_tests(... PROPERTIES
# ENVIRONMENT TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...) in tests/unit_tests/CMakeLists.txt.
#
# RULE: nothing in this file may name a symbol from our own code. Our code is
# the signal TSan exists to give us - above all the SpscQueue, whose whole
# point is that TSan proves the acquire/release pairing. Suppressing anything
# of ours would hide the one result this build is for.
#
# Every entry must be an uninstrumented third-party library whose internals
# TSan cannot see accurately, with the observed test named.
#
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE. The gRPC/Abseil/ZeroMQ entries this file used to carry
# belonged to the consolidated-book project and those libraries are no longer
# dependencies. The remaining uninstrumented libraries are Boost
# (Asio/Beast) and OpenSSL; whether they produce false positives here has NOT
# been observed yet, and inventing a suppression for a race nobody has seen
# would risk hiding a real one. Add entries only when a false positive is
# actually reproduced, and record the test that produced it.
